      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T14:22:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks.\n\nI can\u0027t quite tell whether Mike thought there was a real issue with mem-copying sk_sps, or just didn\u0027t want to argue with the compiler because the non-memcopy code is good enough.  I suspect it\u0027s the latter?\n\nHe\u0027s prolly right about that, the only reason this piqued my interest is I was looking at uninlining checkRealloc and it\u0027s much more tractable for MEM_MOVE\u003dtrue types.\n\nBut even that is speculative at this point, I\u0027m guessing we could maybe save 20-30KB at best.  So if there\u0027s anything iffy about this, it might not be worth pursuing.",
